;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljs:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved
;; (all rows were fetched and byte-matched on 2026-08-22).
;;
;; THREE independent authorities are cited, not one:
;;   * GLEIF, the global LEI system
;;   * the United States, via the SEC's EDGAR submissions API (CVS Health
;;     Corporation is a domestic operating filer, ticker CVS on the NYSE,
;;     CIK 0000064803)
;;   * the issuer itself, at its own published website www.cvshealth.com -- the
;;     terms page this repository archives (80-data/public/tos.journal.edn
;;     archives https://www.cvshealth.com/terms-of-use.html, the same URL the
;;     issuer-* rows cite)
;;
;; WHY NO DELAWARE STATE REGISTER IS CITED DIRECTLY. GLEIF names RA000602 --
;; the Division of Corporations, Department of State, Delaware -- as BOTH the
;; register of record and the validation authority for this entity (rows
;; gleif-registered-at, gleif-validated-at), and the registeredAs 2656078 is
;; the Delaware corporate file number. Delaware publishes no per-entity GET
;; URL: per-entity lookups on icis.corp.delaware.gov run behind POST/session
;; flows and certified extracts are paid (see :catalog/unreachable). What the
;; catalog does instead is corroborate the Delaware claims through independent
;; authorities that do answer on stable URLs: GLEIF says US-DE and legal form
;; XTIQ, the ELF code for a Delaware Corporation (rows gleif-jurisdiction,
;; gleif-legal-form, resolved by the gleif-elf-* definition rows) -> the SEC
;; prints stateOfIncorporation DE (row sec-state-incorp). GLEIF records the
;; file number 2656078 three times (registeredAs, validatedAs, and inside the
;; OpenCorporates id us_de\/2656078 -- rows gleif-registered-as,
;; gleif-validated-as, gleif-ocid). The SEC and GLEIF never consulted each
;; other.
;;
;; FOUR HONEST WRINKLES, SO A READER DOES NOT MISREAD THEM AS DRIFT:
;;   1. GLEIF prints the SAME Delaware registered-agent address -- Corporation
;;      Trust Center, 1209 Orange St, Wilmington DE 19801, care of The
;;      Corporation Trust Company -- as BOTH the legal address AND the
;;      headquarters address (rows gleif-legal-address, gleif-hq-address,
;;      gleif-city, gleif-postal). The operating headquarters is One CVS
;;      Drive, Woonsocket, Rhode Island 02895, and it is visible ONLY from the
;;      SEC (rows sec-street, sec-city, sec-state-ri, sec-zip). The two
;;      authorities do not disagree about a fact -- they answer different
;;      questions ("legal seat" vs "business address"), and each row cites
;;      exactly what its own source prints.
;;   2. The name history is corroborated across both registers WITHOUT a
;;      shared source: GLEIF carries "CVS Caremark Corporation" as a
;;      PREVIOUS_LEGAL_NAME (rows gleif-previous-name, gleif-prev-name-type);
;;      the SEC's formerNames array prints the operative window for
;;      "CVS CAREMARK CORP" (2006-12-27 to 2014-09-03, row
;;      sec-former-caremark) and reaches two names further back than GLEIF:
;;      CVS CORP until 2007 and MELVILLE CORP until 1997 (rows
;;      sec-former-cvs-corp, sec-former-melville). GLEIF's entity creationDate
;;      1996-08-22 (row gleif-creation-date) sits exactly at the Melville ->
;;      CVS restructuring the SEC's windows imply.
;;   3. GLEIF records a COMPLETED CHANGE_LEGAL_NAME event with effectiveDate
;;      2025-12-28, recorded 2026-02-22 (rows gleif-name-change-event,
;;      gleif-name-change-effective). Those dates do NOT match the SEC's
;;      2014 Caremark window in wrinkle 2 -- GLEIF late-recorded the event
;;      under its own bookkeeping dates. Both rows cite only what GLEIF
;;      prints; the SEC row carries the operative window.
;;   4. "mic":null (row gleif-mic-null): unlike the sibling catalog for
;;      Intercontinental Exchange (5493000F4ZO33MV32P92), which maps to MIC
;;      XNYS because that issuer OPERATES an exchange, CVS Health merely LISTS
;;      on the NYSE (row sec-exchange). A null is cited deliberately: it is
;;      the absence that distinguishes a listed company from an exchange
;;      operator.
;;
;; THE AETNA / CVS PHARMACY GROUP STRUCTURE IS VISIBLE FROM TWO AUTHORITIES.
;; GLEIF's relationship graph records 74 direct children for this LEI
;; (retrieved 2026-08-22 on a single page); among them CVS Pharmacy, Inc.,
;; CVS Caremark Indemnity Ltd., and SILVERSCRIPT INSURANCE COMPANY (rows
;; gleif-child-*, cited on the one-page ?page[size]=100 URL so pagination
;; order cannot fake a drift). The issuer's own site header prints the Aetna
;; brand as a first-class property (row issuer-aetna-brand). Child names may
;; legitimately churn as GLEIF relationship records renew; if a gleif-child-*
;; row drifts, re-retrieve the children URL before concluding anything.
;;
;; ROWS THAT WERE DELIBERATELY NOT RECORDED. nextRenewalDate and
;; lastUpdateDate (GLEIF) drift by design on every annual renewal; the terms
;; page's "Last Updated" line drifts on every republication; and
;; https://www.sec.gov/files/company_tickers.json answers 403 to this gate's
;; User-Agent (measured 2026-08-22) although it answers 200 to browser agents
;; -- the ticker<->CIK mapping is instead proven inside the submissions
;; document itself (rows sec-cik, sec-ticker in one body). A catalog row that
;; is expected to change, or whose host refuses the gate, is not a citation --
;; it is a scheduled false alarm.

